<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows10.0.19041.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>Velnix.DecodeHost</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Velnix.DecodeHost</AssemblyName>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <WarningsAsErrors>Nullable</WarningsAsErrors>
    <Platforms>AnyCPU;x64</Platforms>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Constitution v1.1 requires FFmpeg as an LGPL dynamic-link dependency
    (no static linking, no GPL components enabled in the build). We do not
    P/Invoke FFmpeg by hand here: FFmpeg.AutoGen is bindings generated
    directly from FFmpeg's own C headers per targeted version, which is
    the safer choice over hand-written struct layouts (AVFrame and
    AVCodecContext are large, version-sensitive structs; a wrong manual
    offset corrupts memory silently rather than failing loudly).

    This package supplies only the managed P/Invoke signatures. It does
    NOT ship the native FFmpeg binaries. Per the Constitution's LGPL
    dynamic-linking requirement, an LGPL-configured FFmpeg shared build
    (avcodec-*.dll, avformat-*.dll, avutil-*.dll, swscale-*.dll,
    swresample-*.dll) must be placed next to the app executable at
    runtime. See NOTES.md in this folder for acquisition details and the
    version this was written against.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="FFmpeg.AutoGen" Version="8.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Core\Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Playback\Playback.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    LGPL FFmpeg shared-build DLLs (avutil-60.dll, avcodec-62.dll,
    avformat-62.dll, swresample-6.dll, swscale-9.dll — see the comment
    above and NOTES.md for the exact versions this is pinned against).

    CHANGED (2026-08-08): this used to CopyToOutputDirectory, which
    propagates transitively to every consuming project's own bin
    (DecodeHarness, Velnix.App, and DecodeHost's own bin): 3 physical
    copies of ~134MB each. Removed. The 5 real DLLs live ONLY in the
    "ffmpeg" folder next to this .csproj now. FFmpegNativeBootstrap
    resolves that one folder directly via the VELNIX_FFMPEG_DIR
    environment variable (see FFmpegNativeBootstrap.cs) instead of
    expecting a per-exe copy. Set VELNIX_FFMPEG_DIR once on the dev
    machine; see FFMPEG_SHARED_LOCATION_NOTES.md.

    Packaged/shipped builds still need the DLLs physically next to the
    installed exe (Windows LoadLibrary/installer concern, not a dev-time
    build concern): that's a one-time packaging step, not something
    every local `dotnet build` should redo 3x.
  -->

</Project>
